# Docker reads this from the build context, and `docker-compose.yml` points the web
# service at `./apps/web` — not the repo root. A `.dockerignore` sitting at the root
# would be read by nothing, which is why this one lives beside its Dockerfile.

# 1.9 GB of a 1.9 GB context, shipped to the daemon on every `docker compose up
# --build` — four times a batch, now that this repo works as four agents with an
# isolated stack each. It is also a correctness fix and not only a fast one: the
# Dockerfile installs node_modules for linux in the `deps` stage, and the `COPY . .`
# on the line after used to lay the host's darwin-arm64 tree back over it.
node_modules

# Build output. `pnpm build` writes its own inside the image; a copy carried in from
# the host can only be an older answer that Next then believes.
.next
out
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Not inputs to the image. The secrets one matters most: `COPY . .` would put a local
# `.env` into a build layer, and nothing in this Dockerfile ever wanted it there —
# the API origin arrives as a build arg, everything else is runtime environment.
.env
.env.local
.git
.claude
test-results
playwright-report
